course: dictionary
lesson: 4684
title: Homelessness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Homelessness is a noun. It means having no home, or no safe, regular place to live. The ending -ness turns the word into the name of a state or condition, like kindness or sadness.
explain: Context helps you check the meaning. Look at the phrases «tackle homelessness» and «end homelessness». You tackle and end a problem, not a thing you like. So homelessness is a problem that people want to solve, and it is about people who do not have a home.
explain: The word can mean one person's situation, or a problem across a whole town or country. Read the nearby words to see which one fits. Use kind words for people, too: the official US phrase is «Person experiencing homelessness», which means a homeless person.
fact: Homelessness means having no home or no safe, regular place to live.
fact: Homelessness can also mean the problem of many people having no homes in a town or country.
fact: «Tackle homelessness» means to deal with the problem of people having no home.
fact: A «homelessness charity» is a charity that helps people who have no home.
fact: «Person experiencing homelessness» is an official US phrase that means a homeless person.
exercise: «Charities work hard to end homelessness.» What does homelessness mean? | A type of summer holiday | *Having no home or safe place to live | A new way to build roads | Having too many houses to count
exercise: What does «homelessness charity» mean? | A shop that sells houses | A school for builders | A club for people who love moving house | *A charity that helps people who have no home
exercise: What does «Person experiencing homelessness» mean? | A person who builds new homes | A person who is moving to a new town | *A homeless person | A person who sells houses
test: «The town wants to tackle homelessness.» What does the town want to do? | Hold a big party for new homes | *Deal with the problem of people having no home | Build a bigger road | Move all its houses away
test: What does it mean when a whole country has a problem of homelessness? | *Many people in the country have no safe place to live | The country has no buildings at all | Nobody in the country has ever moved | Everyone in the country has two homes
exam: «The council wants to end homelessness.» What is the council hoping for? | More people to move away from town | Houses to be painted a new colour | Empty streets with no people at all | *Everyone has a safe, regular place to live
